  "description": "YUHREZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C63 H99 Dy3 Fe7 N25 O26,7(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.233-3.890 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.38-144.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy3Fe7(μ4-O)2(μ3-OH)2(mdea)7(μ-benzoate)4(N3)6]·2H2O·7CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
